 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# R-Build v2.1 — interactive demo\\n",
    "\\n",
    "R-Build: fully interactive, modifiable open-source LLM architecture + training-speed-boosting library.\\n",
    "Pipeline: **single cache-pull loop line → parallel token-generating layers bundled → next parallel stage**.\\n",
    "\\n",
    "**v2.1 adds full vision-language support** (images & video) plus a ready-made training script (`examples/train_rhododendron_lite.py`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install (GitHub: download the 2.1.0 wheel from the repo, then pip install it)\\n",
    "!pip -q install \\"torch>=2.3\\" \\"numpy>=1.26\\" \\"ipywidgets>=8.0\\"\\n",
    "# !wget -q https://github.com/<you>/rbuild-engine/raw/main/dist/rbuild_engine-2.1.0-py3-none-any.whl\\n",
    "# !pip -q install ./rbuild_engine-2.1.0-py3-none-any.whl"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from rbuild import RBuildConfig, RBuildLM, RBuildTokenizer, Trainer, count_parameters, preset, interactive"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 1. Launch the interactive builder (every value modifiable)"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cfg, panel = interactive.launch()  # edit model / cache_loop / parallel / memory / vision / train, then click Apply"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 2. Build from a scale preset and inspect cost (naive vs optimized)"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cfg = preset(\\"s1\\")           # counter-verified 19.9B total / 3.3B active\\n",
    "print(count_parameters(cfg))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from rbuild import cost_report\\n",
    "print(cost_report(cfg, steps=100_000, seq_len=4096, tokens_per_step=32768))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 3. Train (toy data) — MoD + fine-grained MoE + Muon + WSD + chunked CE + delta-rule memory"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\\n",
    "cfg = RBuildConfig()\\n",
    "cfg.model.vocab_size = 512\\n",
    "model = RBuildLM(cfg)\\n",
    "tok = RBuildTokenizer()\\n",
    "batches = [[tok.encode(\\"the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog\\")] for _ in range(300)]\\n",
    "trainer = Trainer(model, cfg)\\n",
    "hist = trainer.fit(batches, steps=50, log_every=10)\\n",
    "hist[-3:]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 4. Interactive chat (instruct-style, cache-pull loop active)"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "interactive.chat(model, tok, cfg)  # commands: /remember /temp /topp /topk /maxn /forget /config /quit"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4b. VL mode (v2.1)\\n",
    "Enable the vision tower, splice image soft-tokens at `<image>` placeholders, train or generate."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\\n",
    "from rbuild import preset, RBuildLM, count_parameters\\n",
    "\\n",
    "vcfg = preset(\\"s1\\")\\n",
    "vcfg.model.vocab_size = 2048          # demo-size vocab\\n",
    "vcfg.vision.enabled = True\\n",
    "vcfg.vision.image_token_id = 128001   # reserved <|image|> placeholder id in your tokenizer\\n",
    "\\n",
    "vmodel = RBuildLM(vcfg)\\n",
    "print(count_parameters(vcfg))         # counter-verified: vision params included\\n",
    "\\n",
    "tpi = (vcfg.vision.image_size // vcfg.vision.patch_size) ** 2   # tokens per image = (224/14)^2 = 256\\n",
    "ids = torch.randint(0, 2048, (1, 24))\\n",
    "ids[0, 5:5+tpi] = vcfg.vision.image_token_id                    # splice one image placeholder run\\n",
    "images = torch.randn(1, 1, 3, vcfg.vision.image_size, vcfg.vision.image_size)  # (B, N, C, H, W); N>1 = video\\n",
    "\\n",
    "out = vmodel(ids, images=images)      # forward with vision spliced in\\n",
    "print(\\"logits:\\\", out[\\"logits\\"].shape)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Blind mode (default): vision.enabled=False -> zero vision params, pure text."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 5. Notes\\n- `interactive.launch()` falls back to console prompts outside Jupyter.\\n- Cost report is always two columns: naive baseline vs R-Build optimized.\\n- Blind (text-only) by default; flip `cfg.vision.enabled = True` for VL. `freeze_vision=True` trains only the projector."]
  }
 ],
